            <ArticleTitle>[Chronic left ventricular pseudoaneurism of undetermined etiology].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e4-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0066-782X2010000100024</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pseudoaneurysms occur as a rare complication of the myocardial infarction, of which hemorrhagic process is contained by adherences of the visceral or parietal pericardium - or of both - preventing the development of cardiac tamponade. We report the case of a 55-year-old patient, with a chronic left ventricular pseudoaneurysm of undetermined etiology, who was submitted to a conservative treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
